Little CPU
==========

Little CPU is an implementation of RV32IMAC_Zicsr_Zifencei (machine mode only) in SystemVerilog.

You can run the test suite by installing yosys, icarus-verilog and a RISC-V cross compiler.
On macOS, brew installs the first two and `make setup` the third, and then the suite is just a
make away:

  brew install yosys icarus-verilog
  make setup
  make test

It is formally verified with: https://github.com/YosysHQ/riscv-formal

To run the formal checks install the YosysHQ OSS CAD Suite (which includes SymbiYosys) from:
https://github.com/YosysHQ/oss-cad-suite-build

And then run:

  make -C formal check
  make -C formal complete

I'm unreasonably proud and excited by this project, it was made with love, and I hope that it is a
good read. There's much more to come!
